    era: "Foundational Giants",    image: "/images/scientists/nikola-tesla.jpg",
    bio: "Nikola Tesla was born in Smiljan, Croatia, then part of the Austrian Empire, during a lightning storm \u2014 an omen, his mother reportedly said. He had an eidetic memory and could visualize inventions in complete detail before building them. He studied engineering in Graz and Prague before working for the Continental Edison Company in Paris.\n\nIn 1884, Tesla arrived in New York with four cents in his pocket. He briefly worked for Thomas Edison before they famously fell out over payment. Tesla developed the alternating current (AC) induction motor and polyphase system of electrical distribution \u2014 the foundation of the modern electrical grid. His battle with Edison over AC vs DC became known as the 'War of Currents,' which Tesla won decisively.\n\nAt his laboratory in Colorado Springs, Tesla claimed to have transmitted electricity wirelessly through the earth. His Wardenclyffe Tower on Long Island was intended to demonstrate wireless power transmission across the Atlantic, but funding dried up. Tesla died penniless in a New York hotel room in 1943. The SI unit of magnetic flux density is named the 'tesla' in his honor. Elon Musk named his electric car company after him.",
